<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="any">
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href="/images/favicon-32.png">
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="16x16" href="/images/favicon-16.png">
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="180x180" href="/images/apple-touch-icon.png">
    <title>LowEndInsight - OSS Supply Chain Risk Analysis</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Open source supply chain risk analysis for any public git repository. Agents pay per use over the Machine Payments Protocol, with no account.">
    <%# The same guide, as markdown, for agents that read /llms.txt rather than HTML. %>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/markdown" href="/llms.txt" title="LowEndInsight for agents">
    <link rel="describedby" type="application/json" href="/openapi.json">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bulma@0.9.4/css/bulma.min.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/theme.css">
    <script>
      // Inline and synchronous on purpose: a deferred script runs after first
      // paint, and the flash of the wrong theme is the thing being avoided.
      (function () {
        try {
          var t = localStorage.getItem("lei-theme");
          if (t) document.documentElement.setAttribute("data-theme", t);
        } catch (e) {}
      })();
    </script>
    <script type="text/javascript" defer src="https://use.fontawesome.com/releases/v5.3.1/js/all.js"></script>
    <style>
      body { background: var(--bg); }
      .hero-body { padding-bottom: 1rem; }
      pre { background: var(--pre-bg); color: var(--pre-text); border-radius: 6px; padding: 1.25rem; overflow-x: auto; }
      
      
      
      code { color: var(--code-text); background: var(--code-bg); padding: 0.15em 0.4em; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 0.9em; }
      pre code { color: inherit; background: none; padding: 0; }
      .endpoint { font-family: monospace; font-weight: bold; }
      .steps li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <section class="hero is-dark is-small">
      <div class="hero-body">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="columns is-vcentered">
            <div class="column is-narrow">
              <img src="/images/lei_bus_128.png" alt="LEI" style="max-height:64px;">
            </div>
            <div class="column">
              <h1 class="title">LowEndInsight</h1>
              <p class="subtitle">Open source supply chain risk and agentic analysis</p>
            </div>
            <div class="column is-narrow">
              <a class="button is-primary is-outlined" href="#agents">
                <span class="icon"><i class="fas fa-robot"></i></span>
                <span>For agents</span>
              </a>
              <a class="button is-success is-outlined" href="/signup">
                <span class="icon"><i class="fas fa-user-plus"></i></span>
                <span>Signup</span>
              </a>
              <a class="button is-info is-outlined" href="/login">
                <span class="icon"><i class="fas fa-sign-in-alt"></i></span>
                <span>Login</span>
              </a>
              <a class="button is-warning is-outlined" href="/doc">
                <span class="icon"><i class="fas fa-book-open"></i></span>
                <span>API Docs</span>
              </a>
              <a class="button is-light is-outlined" href="https://github.com/kitplummer/lowendinsight" target="_blank">
                <span class="icon"><i class="fab fa-github"></i></span>
                <span>Source</span>
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="columns">
          <div class="column is-8">
            <div class="box" id="agents">
              <h2 class="title is-4">Use it from an agent &mdash; no account needed</h2>
              <p class="mb-4">LowEndInsight is paid per use over the <a href="https://mpp.dev">Machine Payments Protocol</a> (MPP), an open HTTP payment scheme. An agent that has never been here can analyze a repository without signing up: it asks, is told the price, pays, and is served.</p>

              <ol class="steps ml-5 mb-4">
                <li><strong>Ask.</strong> <code>POST /v1/analyze</code> with no credentials returns <code>402 Payment Required</code> and a <code>WWW-Authenticate: Payment</code> challenge naming the amount, the asset and where to send it.</li>
                <li><strong>Pay and retry the same request</strong> with <code>Authorization: Payment &lt;credential&gt;</code>. An MPP client does both steps for you.</li>
                <li><strong>Receive</strong> the analysis, a <code>Payment-Receipt</code>, and a <code>Lei-Api-Key</code>.</li>
                <li><strong>Come back</strong> with <code>Authorization: Bearer lei_&hellip;</code> and spend the balance without paying again.</li>
              </ol>

              <%= if guide.live? do %>
                <p class="notification is-info is-light">Stablecoin payments use <strong><%= guide.stablecoin.token %></strong> on <strong><%= guide.stablecoin.chain %></strong>, settled through Stripe.</p>
              <% else %>
                <p class="notification is-warning is-light"><strong>Payments are in test mode.</strong> Stablecoin payments use <%= guide.stablecoin.token %> on <%= guide.stablecoin.chain %>, and no real money moves.</p>
              <% end %>

              <%= unless guide.stablecoin.available? do %>
                <p class="notification is-danger is-light">Stablecoin payment is not available right now. A request without credentials receives a <code>402</code> saying so, and is not served.</p>
              <% end %>

              <h3 class="title is-5">What the first request returns</h3>
              <pre><code>curl -i -X POST https://lowendinsight.dev/v1/analyze \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"urls": ["https://github.com/kitplummer/clikan"]}'

HTTP/2 402
www-authenticate: Payment id="&hellip;", realm="lowendinsight.dev",
  method="tempo", intent="charge", request="&hellip;"</code></pre>

              <h3 class="title is-5 mt-5">Paying with an MPP client</h3>
              <pre><code>import { Mppx, tempo } from 'mppx/client'

const mppx = Mppx.create({ methods: [tempo({ account })], polyfill: false })

const res = await mppx.fetch('https://lowendinsight.dev/v1/analyze', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({ urls: ['https://github.com/kitplummer/clikan'] }),
})

const key = res.headers.get('lei-api-key')   // keep it: it holds your balance</code></pre>
              <p class="is-size-7">A machine-readable version of this guide is at <a href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a>.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="box" id="pricing">
              <h2 class="title is-4">Pricing</h2>
              <table class="table is-fullwidth">
                <tbody>
                  <tr><td>A repository with a cached report</td><td><strong><%= LowendinsightGet.AgentGuide.number(guide.hit_credits) %> credits</strong></td><td><%= guide.hit_usd %></td></tr>
                  <tr><td>A repository analyzed fresh</td><td><strong><%= LowendinsightGet.AgentGuide.number(guide.miss_credits) %> credits</strong></td><td><%= guide.miss_usd %></td></tr>
                  <tr><td>A block, bought when an agent's balance runs out</td><td><strong><%= LowendinsightGet.AgentGuide.number(guide.top_up_credits) %> credits</strong></td><td><%= guide.top_up_usd %></td></tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
              <p class="is-size-7">One credit is $0.001. A cached report is cheaper because someone has already paid for the work: every analysis makes the next request for that repository cheaper, whoever makes it.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="box" id="payment-options">
              <h2 class="title is-4">Ways to pay</h2>
              <div class="table-container">
                <table class="table is-fullwidth">
                  <thead>
                    <tr><th>Pathway</th><th>For</th><th>How</th><th>Now</th></tr>
                  </thead>
                  <tbody>
                    <tr>
                      <td><strong>Stablecoin</strong><br><span class="is-size-7">MPP <code>tempo</code></span></td>
                      <td>Any agent, no account</td>
                      <td>Transfer <%= guide.stablecoin.token %> on <%= guide.stablecoin.chain %> to the address in the challenge. Stripe verifies and settles it.</td>
                      <td><%= if guide.stablecoin.available?, do: "Available", else: "Unavailable" %></td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td><strong>Card through an agent wallet</strong><br><span class="is-size-7">MPP <code>stripe</code>, Shared Payment Token</span></td>
                      <td>Agents with an API key</td>
                      <td>A Shared Payment Token from an agent wallet such as Link. Not offered without an account: a card token identifies no one to hold the balance.</td>
                      <td><%= if guide.card.available?, do: "Available", else: "Unavailable" %></td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td><strong>Free tier</strong></td>
                      <td>People</td>
                      <td><a href="/signup">Sign up</a> for an API key: <%= LowendinsightGet.AgentGuide.number(guide.free_monthly_analyses) %> analyses a month.</td>
                      <td>Available</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td><strong>Pro</strong></td>
                      <td>People</td>
                      <td><a href="/signup">Sign up</a> and subscribe through Stripe Checkout: <%= guide.pro_price %>, including <%= guide.pro_included_usd %> of usage.</td>
                      <td>Available</td>
                    </tr>
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="box">
              <h2 class="title is-4">With an API key</h2>
              <h3 class="title is-5">Analyze a repo</h3>
              <pre><code>curl -X POST https://lowendinsight.dev/v1/analyze \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer lei_&hellip;" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"urls": ["https://github.com/kitplummer/clikan"]}'</code></pre>

              <h3 class="title is-5 mt-5">Check a job result</h3>
              <pre><code>curl https://lowendinsight.dev/v1/analyze/{uuid}</code></pre>

              <h3 class="title is-5 mt-5">Analyze an SBOM</h3>
              <pre><code>curl -X POST https://lowendinsight.dev/v1/analyze/sbom \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer lei_&hellip;" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"sbom": &lt;cyclonedx-or-spdx-json&gt;}'</code></pre>
            </div>

            <div class="box">
              <h2 class="title is-4">API Endpoints</h2>
              <table class="table is-fullwidth">
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th>Method</th>
                    <th>Path</th>
                    <th>Description</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <td><span class="tag tag-green">POST</span></td>
                    <td class="endpoint">/v1/analyze</td>
                    <td>Submit URLs for analysis (blocking, async, or stale mode)</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><span class="tag is-info">GET</span></td>
                    <td class="endpoint">/v1/analyze/{uuid}</td>
                    <td>Retrieve analysis results by job UUID</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><span class="tag tag-green">POST</span></td>
                    <td class="endpoint">/v1/analyze/sbom</td>
                    <td>Analyze repos from a CycloneDX or SPDX SBOM</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><span class="tag is-info">GET</span></td>
                    <td class="endpoint">/v1/cache/export</td>
                    <td>Export cache for air-gapped deployment</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><span class="tag tag-green">POST</span></td>
                    <td class="endpoint">/v1/cache/import</td>
                    <td>Import pre-warmed cache</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><span class="tag is-info">GET</span></td>
                    <td class="endpoint">/v1/cache/stats</td>
                    <td>Cache statistics</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
              <p>See the full <a href="/doc">interactive API documentation</a> for request/response schemas and examples.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="column is-4">
            <div class="box" id="no-account">
              <h2 class="title is-5">No account, and why</h2>
              <div class="content">
                <p>An agent has no signup, email or organization to give, and asking for one would turn away the consumers this service is built for. <strong>The payment is the identity:</strong> the wallet that paid holds the balance.</p>
                <p><strong>What we keep:</strong> money and counts. Each purchase and debit is recorded with the paying wallet and the amount, the financial record of what was paid and spent. We also keep monthly analysis counts.</p>
                <p><strong>What we don't keep:</strong> which repositories a wallet analyzed. They aren't recorded against the payer, and routine production logs don't name them.</p>
                <p><strong>Reports are cached by repository, not by who asked.</strong> That is what makes a cached report cheaper for everyone.</p>
                <p><strong>No free allowance for wallets.</strong> A wallet costs nothing to create, so a free allowance per wallet would be a free allowance per attacker. Access comes from credits.</p>
                <p class="is-size-7">A stablecoin transfer is public on the <%= guide.stablecoin.chain %> chain, as every on-chain payment is. What it paid for is not.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="box">
              <h2 class="title is-5">Risk Indicators</h2>
              <div class="content">
                <ul>
                  <li><strong>Contributor count</strong> &mdash; bus factor risk</li>
                  <li><strong>Contributor risk</strong> &mdash; overall contributor risk level</li>
                  <li><strong>Functional contributors</strong> &mdash; concentration of commits</li>
                  <li><strong>Functional contributors risk</strong> &mdash; contributor concentration risk level</li>
                  <li><strong>Commit currency</strong> &mdash; weeks since last commit</li>
                  <li><strong>Commit currency risk</strong> &mdash; staleness risk level</li>
                  <li><strong>Large recent commit risk</strong> &mdash; codebase volatility</li>
                  <li><strong>Recent commit size %</strong> &mdash; last commit as % of codebase</li>
                  <li><strong>SBOM risk</strong> &mdash; dependency/supply chain risk</li>
                  <li><strong>Agentic classification</strong> &mdash; <code>human</code> / <code>mixed</code> / <code>agent</code> based on bot/AI commit ratio</li>
                  <li><strong>Agentic contribution ratio</strong> &mdash; fraction of commits from bots or AI agents (0.0&ndash;1.0)</li>
                  <li><strong>Restricted contributors</strong> &mdash; whether any contributors have restricted GitHub profiles (requires GitHub token)</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <p class="is-size-7 has-text-grey">Agentic thresholds: <code>human</code> &lt; 0.3, <code>mixed</code> 0.3&ndash;0.7, <code>agent</code> &gt; 0.7</p>
            </div>

            <div class="box">
              <h2 class="title is-5">Agentic Classification</h2>
              <div class="content">
                <p>Each repository is classified based on the ratio of commits attributed to automated or AI contributors:</p>
                <table class="table is-fullwidth is-narrow">
                  <tbody>
                    <tr><td><span class="tag is-success">human</span></td><td>Ratio &lt; 0.3 &mdash; predominantly human-authored</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><span class="tag is-warning">mixed</span></td><td>Ratio &ge; 0.3 &mdash; mix of human and agentic</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><span class="tag is-danger">agent</span></td><td>Ratio &ge; 0.7 &mdash; predominantly agentic</td></tr>
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="box">
              <h2 class="title is-5">Risk Levels</h2>
              <table class="table is-fullwidth is-narrow">
                <tbody>
                  <tr><td><span class="tag tag-red">critical</span></td><td>Immediate attention needed</td></tr>
                  <tr><td><span class="tag tag-orange">high</span></td><td>Significant concern</td></tr>
                  <tr><td><span class="tag is-warning">medium</span></td><td>Worth monitoring</td></tr>
                  <tr><td><span class="tag is-success">low</span></td><td>Healthy indicator</td></tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>

            <div class="box">
              <h2 class="title is-5">Try it</h2>
              <form id="form" action="/url=" method="get" onsubmit="return validate_and_submit(event)">
                <div class="field has-addons">
                  <div class="control is-expanded">
                    <input type="text" id="input-url" class="input" placeholder="https://github.com/org/repo" required oninput="remove_error()">
                  </div>
                  <div class="control">
                    <button type="submit" id="analyze-button" class="button is-dark">Analyze</button>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </form>
              <span id="invalid-url" style="display: none; color: var(--accent-red);">Invalid repo URL</span>
              <p id="try-it-limited" class="is-size-7 mt-2" style="display: none; color: var(--accent-red);">
                This address has used its fresh analyses through the Try It form for now. Reports already analyzed are still free here. For more, use the API: <a href="#agents">pay per use with no account</a>, or <a href="/signup">get a free key</a>.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="box">
              <h2 class="title is-5">Links</h2>
              <div class="content">
                <ul>
                  <li><a href="/llms.txt">Guide for agents (llms.txt)</a></li>
                  <li><a href="/doc">Interactive API Docs (Swagger)</a></li>
                  <li><a href="/openapi.json">OpenAPI Spec (JSON)</a></li>
                  <li><a href="/gh_trending">GitHub Trending Analysis</a></li>
                  <li><a href="https://github.com/kitplummer/lowendinsight">Source Code</a></li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer class="footer" style="padding: 1.5rem;">
      <div class="content has-text-centered">
        <p>LowEndInsight is developed and operated by <a href="https://revolveteam.com"><strong>(r)evolve</strong></a>.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 0.85rem;">Originally created as research at
          <a href="https://gtri.gatech.edu">GTRI</a> &mdash; BSD 3-Clause License</p>
        <p style="font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--text-muted);">v<%= version %></p>
      </div>
    </footer>

    <script src="/js/endpoints.js" type="text/javascript"></script>
      <button id="theme-toggle" class="theme-toggle" type="button">Dark mode</button>
    <script src="/js/theme.js" type="text/javascript"></script>
</body>
</html>
